The main reason I play [S] is because after you get most of the AK in
Vanilla the game is tedious and boring.  There are no real threats
besides the occational Arch-Lich and summoning storm.  And even those
are rare enough, (or geno enough) that you can easily succumb to
auto-pilot mistake.  Actually, I find that's the biggest late game
killer -- just getting lazy and thinking you're invulnerable.

And [S] gives me a nice wakeup call ever time I play.  Right now I
have a character who just did the Neutral and Lawful Quests as well as
the Class Quest.  At this point Vanilla would be all but sewn up.  I
have most of my AK, minus speed boots, and a ring of free-action.  And
normally I could get all the way to the sanctum without noticing the
absence of the latter.  But in [S] I walked into the Crypt or whatever
it's called where all the undead are having a jamboree.  And I see, oh
on Lich, no biggie.  And I happen to be in Xorn from from taking out a
*trice nest.  So waltz in and whamo!  The Ghoul Mage casts a paralysis
spell on me, and forgot I have no MR because I'm a xorn who can't wear
my MR Cloak, and he hits and hits and hits and bye-bye +5 GoP, bye-bye
+4 Helm of Telepathy, I'm down to 1hp and lucky he didn't give me the
Finger.  So I call the all out retreat and now I'm back at HQ licking
my wounds.

[S] has too many (in a good way) nasty spell casters to get lazy.

